<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office over the Friday to Sunday weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final data are due Monday. (Rank last week in parentheses).</p>
<p>    1 (*) Beverly Hills Ninja ............. $10.0 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Metro ............................ $9.3 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Evita ............................ $7.2 million</p>
<p>    4 (5) Jerry Maguire .................... $6.8 million</p>
<p>    5 (1) The Relic ........................ $6.7 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) Scream ........................... $6.3 million</p>
<p>    7 (3) Michael .......................... $6.0 million</p>
<p>    8 (7) The People Vs. Larry Flynt ....... $3.4 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) Jackie Chan's First Strike ....... $2.8 million</p>
<p>    10(9) &quot;Mother&quot; ......................... $2.5 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Beverly Hills Ninja&quot; and &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; are released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Metro&quot; and &quot;Evita&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.  </p>
<p>&quot;The Relic&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; is released by Disney-owned Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Michael&quot; was produced by Turner Pictures, and released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The People Vs. Larry Flynt&quot; is released by Sony-owned Columbia Pictures.</p>
<p>&quot;Jackie Chan's First Strike&quot; is released by New Line.</p>
<p>&quot;Mother&quot; is released by Paramount, which is owned by Viacom Inc.</p>
</text>
